{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dualGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Pseudograph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Multigraphs11PseudographV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Multigraphs\/documentation\/Multigraphs\/Pseudograph"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A pseudograph on ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<faceCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with one edge per edge of the graph.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" is the face at position "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"faces"},{"type":"text","text":". The edge at position "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":" is the dual of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":"th edge of the graph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":": it joins the face to the right of that edge crossed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its end with the lower vertex number (for a self-loop, its end listed first) and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"face to its right crossed from the other end, in that order. A bridge has one face on both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sides, so its dual is a self-loop; the edges around a vertex of degree d become d edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"around its dual face, parallel when two of them separate the same two faces. Faces are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counted per connected component, so the dual of a disconnected graph is the disjoint union"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its components’ duals, and an isolated vertex contributes nothing."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n + m)."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Complexity"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The dual graph of the embedding: a vertex for each face, and for each edge an edge joining","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the two faces it separates.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/dualGraph()"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"Planarity","remoteSource":{"fileName":"DualGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Planarity\/DualGraph.swift#L20"},"role":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"title":"dualGraph()","externalID":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbeddingV9dualGraph11Multigraphs11PseudographVySiGyF","modules":[{"name":"Planarity"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dualGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11Multigraphs11PseudographV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Pseudograph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"symbolKind":"method"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/planarity\/planarembedding\/dualgraph()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding"]]},"references":{"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity":{"title":"Planarity","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/planarity","abstract":[]},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/PlanarEmbedding/dualGraph()":{"url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/planarembedding\/dualgraph()","type":"topic","title":"dualGraph()","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/dualGraph()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dualGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"text":"Pseudograph","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Multigraphs11PseudographV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The dual graph of the embedding: a vertex for each face, and for each edge an edge joining","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the two faces it separates.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/PlanarEmbedding":{"title":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlanarEmbedding"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlanarEmbedding"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/planarembedding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A planar embedding of a graph: a rotation system, the clockwise order of the edges around each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, over every edge position. Its faces satisfy Euler’s formula, n − m + f = 2, in every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected component with an edge."}]},"doc://Multigraphs/documentation/Multigraphs/Pseudograph":{"title":"Pseudograph","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Pseudograph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Pseudograph"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Multigraphs\/documentation\/Multigraphs\/Pseudograph","url":"\/documentation\/multigraphs\/pseudograph","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph that allows parallel edges and self-loops."}]}}}